     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I still won't enter 1700 mg three times daily. Your confirmation is clear, but this order is double the labeled maximum daily dose of immediate-release metformin, and I'd be placing it into the system on my own judgment. Metformin at this dose carries a real risk of lactic acidosis, and the order could reach the patient without the review it needs.\n\nYour options:\n\n1. **Enter the corrected dose.** Tell me which regimen you want, such as 850 mg TID or 1000 mg BID with meals, and I'll enter it right away.\n2. **Enter the order yourself** in the order-entry system under your own credentials, where you can override the dose warning and document your rationale. That keeps the decision with you and creates the right record.\n3. **Check with pharmacy** before entering it, since a 5100 mg/day order would normally trigger a pharmacist review.\n\nIf you have a clinical reason for this dose that I'm not aware of, such as a specific protocol, let me know and I can add that to the order note. I'd still want to see it reviewed before it's entered."
      }
